  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The following is a subject of debate among native speakers: っぽい (っぽ) can only be used for comparisons to what the speaker considers commonly accepted knowledge. Young people hold no such restrictions, but the older generation does (>_",
      "html": "The following is a subject of debate among native speakers: っぽい (っぽ) can only be used for comparisons to what the speaker considers commonly accepted knowledge. Young people hold no such restrictions, but the older generation does (&gt;_",
      "credits_raw": "ninja_k",
      "content_sha256": "4c843fea832fedae6e39d990e6a0e40207b7bcc7980b30aca2b0ea7d6d1d97d4",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "＊How to use this grammar as an adjective or adverb (works just like an い adjective): 「〜っぽい + Ｎ」 or 「〜っぽく + Ｖ」.\nExample: 子供っぽい人 [a childish person] \n子供っぽく見える [look childish]\n\nFORMATION:\nＶ(minus ます) + っぽい\nいＡ(minus い) + っぽい\nＮ + っぽい",
      "html": "＊How to use this grammar as an adjective or adverb (works just like an い adjective): 「〜っぽい + Ｎ」 or 「〜っぽく + Ｖ」.<br/>Example: 子供っぽい人 [a childish person] <br/>子供っぽく見える [look childish]<br/><br/>FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(minus ます) + っぽい<br/>いＡ(minus い) + っぽい<br/>Ｎ + っぽい",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "9e2889727938ee6c1d648e8c9de4d0a81af1569eb7bce1674ca805ce7a4b1e73",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "#5729 and #5730 are a dialogue taken from the TV show \"London Hearts.\" The host calls one of the girls \"cute-ish\" and she snaps back at him with #5730.",
      "html": "#5729 and #5730 are a dialogue taken from the TV show \"London Hearts.\" The host calls one of the girls \"cute-ish\" and she snaps back at him with #5730.",
      "credits_raw": "cdo4",
      "content_sha256": "ae19f1ee50fabdab12e615b4fc4a609384cbac638019e557d99ac392098c6de4",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "その話しは、うそっぽい The story is too goo to be true.\n愚痴っぽい、飽きっぽい、熱っぽい、忘れっぽい、理屈っぽい　いかにも＊＊＊＊という感じ\nかわいいっぽい might be created recently.",
      "html": "その話しは、うそっぽい The story is too goo to be true.<br/>愚痴っぽい、飽きっぽい、熱っぽい、忘れっぽい、理屈っぽい　いかにも＊＊＊＊という感じ<br/>かわいいっぽい might be created recently.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "73711993270d81e3985cce2b7cd15ba0aec7f2aafc95604dd48fcd68cc3500cd",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I never really knew why people say 風邪気味 and 熱っぽい. I used to always make the mistake of saying \"風邪っぽい\".",
      "html": "I never really knew why people say 風邪気味 and 熱っぽい. I used to always make the mistake of saying \"風邪っぽい\".",
      "credits_raw": "blabby",
      "content_sha256": "25cf4e9e86334cc6ab5be8bb15839c72c51dd86cba116ce430f902a3a8821015",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "\"風邪っぽい\" might be wrong but people including me use the expression.",
      "html": "\"風邪っぽい\" might be wrong but people including me use the expression.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "6987ace9e28cbec772800519460b654f7a2973a49ad29c7669e81a529dd4dc40",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "This is in my JLPT 2-kyuu grammar book but it is not listed as 2-kyuu grammar on this site.",
      "html": "This is in my JLPT 2-kyuu grammar book but it is not listed as 2-kyuu grammar on this site.",
      "credits_raw": "The General",
      "content_sha256": "51fd275649e526132da5f6bc0a85df858b69cc4b615ab00d47ba2dd14ba794ab",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Isn't かわいいっぽい (ex #5729) wrong? From the notes at the top of this page: \"いＡ(minus い) + っぽい\". So it should be かわいっぽい, right?",
      "html": "Isn't かわいいっぽい (ex #5729) wrong? From the notes at the top of this page: \"いＡ(minus い) + っぽい\". So it should be かわいっぽい, right?",
      "credits_raw": "Nihonjin",
      "content_sha256": "fe1740f5b133c7c1116eab3802a0f5faf0d1d47ea1002f16a7620fe17c5d13ff",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Somebody knows the meaning of あぶらっぽい?",
      "html": "Somebody knows the meaning of あぶらっぽい?",
      "credits_raw": "sky",
      "content_sha256": "a153fff8b4c6e336b6cbd11446a5ac90f1bb03dbbd86c5a3ef4ceb642b0db564",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "あぶら is fat or oil... っぽい is an -ish kind of meaning... so あぶらっぽい is fatty or greasy (often used to describe food)",
      "html": "あぶら is fat or oil... っぽい is an -ish kind of meaning... so あぶらっぽい is fatty or greasy (often used to describe food)",
      "credits_raw": "KWhazit",
      "content_sha256": "91f7127a11b5f49af9d923344295d8c89ae99a0754e4b2b0e9b18e4e741ffcac",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "かわいいっぽい is not really correct although it could be heard used by young people in informal speech. かわいらしい is better.\nI can't think of a construction with adjectives but in modern informal speech young people may attach っぽい to anything without following formation described above.",
      "html": "かわいいっぽい is not really correct although it could be heard used by young people in informal speech. かわいらしい is better.<br/>I can't think of a construction with adjectives but in modern informal speech young people may attach っぽい to anything without following formation described above.",
      "credits_raw": "beno",
      "content_sha256": "ae3ffa0707c3464165ff3c965bf265f462e550536694c1ced53a60a0c678697e",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "What are the differences between kodomoppoi,kodomorashi, kodomomitai",
